INT. BALLROOM CLOAKROOM - ART DECO HOTEL - NIGHT

A narrow room of brass hooks and furs. A single frosted lamp. Muffled orchestra through the wall.

A WOMAN in a sapphire gown leans against the counter, breathing hard. Her lipstick is smeared. Her hand grips a champagne flute so tightly it might break.

The attendant's stool is empty.

The door opens. Another WOMAN steps in, in a silver gown, a fur stole over one arm. She closes the door behind her. Locks it.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
You followed me.

WOMAN IN SILVER
You left your wrap.

She holds out a stole. The woman in sapphire stares at it. Doesn't take it.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
I said I wouldn't dance.

WOMAN IN SILVER
You danced with him.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
She asked.

WOMAN IN SILVER
She did?

The sapphire woman sets the flute down. It rings on the marble.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
Constance asked me for the third waltz. In front of everyone. I couldn't say no.

WOMAN IN SILVER
Of course you could.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
She's my cousin.

WOMAN IN SILVER
She's your cousin who looks at you like I do.

Silence. The orchestra swells and falls.

The woman in silver steps closer and drapes the stole over her companion's shoulders. For a moment they stand with their foreheads almost touching.

WOMAN IN SAPPHIRE
I'm Ottoline, by the way. You never asked.

OTTOLINE
(softer)
Ottoline Fairbrother-Nnamdi.

WOMAN IN SILVER
Marguerite.

OTTOLINE
Marguerite, I'm terrified.

MARGUERITE
Good. So am I.

A knock at the door. They break apart. Ottoline wipes her lipstick. Marguerite unlocks the door and opens it on the roar of the band.
